{"name":"Night Train","hex":"#4b7689","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"},{"term":"train","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Elongated or trailing portion.","A trail or line of something, especially gunpowder."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To practice an ability.","To teach and form (someone) by practice; to educate (someone)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/train"}],"entries":[{"title":"Night Train (painting)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Train is a 1947 painting by Belgian artist Paul Delvaux, famous for his paintings of female nudes. The painting is 153 × 210 centimetres and is now in the Museum of Modern Art, in Toyama, in Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b4/Le_train_de_nuit.jpg/330px-Le_train_de_nuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Train_(painting)"},{"title":"Night Train (Jason Aldean album)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Train is the fifth studio album by American country music artist Jason Aldean. It was released on October 16, 2012, via Broken Bow Records. The album features a collaboration with Luke Bryan and Eric Church on \"The Only Way I Know\". It was produced by Michael Knox and features Aldean's road band, with songs written by various songwriters."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/NightTrainAldean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Train_(Jason_Aldean_album)"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b4/Le_train_de_nuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b4/Le_train_de_nuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALe_train_de_nuit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/NightTrainAldean.jpg/250px-NightTrainAldean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/NightTrainAldean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/NightTrainAldean.jpg/250px-NightTrainAldean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANightTrainAldean.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/500px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki